 returns explicit unavailable/null instead of a fabricated empty account. Human and Agent statistics
 share the same query owner and scope semantics.
+
+### Verified connection status and targeted failure feedback
+
+Registry executable means configuration can be submitted, not that authentication or inference has
+succeeded. Imported/saved connections start unverified. Only an actual completed probe may mark the
+specific tested model successful; failed/late checks cannot leave a green ready signal. UI probe
+observations include the tested model/time and expire when their host, committed configuration revision or settings mount changes. They are not durable account health facts.
+
+Retain the existing model network failure's status/reason/business code through the connectivity
+RPC as a bounded typed result, not a string-only exception. Classify authentication, explicit expired
+subscription/quota, unsupported client, absent model/endpoint, request format/parameters, timeout,
+network and provider failures without guessing expiry from 401/403. Localize summaries and next steps.
+Test failures use the original inline feedback owner; model metadata opens only on explicit edit.
+
+Acceptance: a loopback-only fixture replays the recorded Kimi `access_terminated_error` through the
+built desktop, Host, CLI and actual AI SDK stream path. The Chinese/English message identifies
+missing subscription service access, retains HTTP 403, marks the probe failed and leaves metadata
+closed. A complete synthetic successful stream marks only its tested model successful. Original
+review-profile credentials, default and model parameters are preserved; no paid probe was sent.
